Subject: [#94-9-561] The fruits of others' labor

One of the real problems with left-anarchy is that no clear procedure 
emerges as to who is responsible for and ultimately has the authority to 
make decisions regarding resources and means of production.

Yeah, we can imagine the workers owning a particular plant or company in
an overall capitalist economy, and even being successful, but I defy you
to describe how an overall socialist-anarchist system would work unless
you end-up with a heirarchical "one big union" controlled either from the
top by those manipulating the "vote" or real, bottom-up democracy.  I say
this is still Statism, worse statism in fact than our current State
capitalism. 

In capitalism the owner's "job" is to make the ultimate decision about 
how his property is to be used.  Even if he delegates management to 
professionals, it is still ultimately his or her authority that is being 
used to allocate resources.  And the owner chooses to who he/she delegates.

This system works and can be described.

As an anarcho-capitalist, I would like to reduce or eliminate the ability
of ruling class property owners to use the state to maintain and enlarge
their ownership via special privileges, licensing, manipulated
regulations, central banking, unfair taxes, etc.  This could be achieved
through greater education of the populace regarding economic cause and
effect.  Most social legislation, entitlements, regulation, Central
Banking, etc. actually favors the large ruling class Established firms
with special ties to the State at the expense of newcomers and small
business and true co-operatives. 

The way people interact on this list (anarchy-list and all others for that
matter) is proof enough if any were actually needed that people are
inherently competitive.  An anarchist future that eliminates competition
between individuals and/or communes is just hopeless in my opinion and
misses the real opportunity to reduce or eliminate the current extreme
concentration of capital in the ruling class. 

